message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the article given under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "Neural gate control of the South Mirzachul main canal under supply shortage: code, data and results"
abstract: >-
  Code, input data, trained controllers and simulation results for the article
  "Equitable Water Distribution in a Large Irrigation Canal under Supply Shortage
  Using Neural Gate Control Trained on a Saint-Venant Model". The study tests
  whether a neural supervisory controller can share a supply shortage more
  equitably among the offtakes of the 123.7-km South Mirzachul main canal
  (Uzbekistan). It operates only gates that the canal already has: seven check
  gates, the tail gate and the regulators of five major branches. Everything
  runs on a one-dimensional Saint-Venant model of the canal built from its
  passport. The repository contains everything needed to rebuild Tables 1–4
  and Figs. 2–8 of the article. Code: MIT licence; data, results and figures:
  CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).
